\par
Choose \lquote Don't Use\rquote , and they will follow whatever tactics you've set without using pep powers.\par
\par
This setting can also be altered in battle.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b Exchanging Equipment in the Heat of Battle\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 You can mix up what you're wearing and wielding even while battling baddies.\par
\par
Simply select \lquote Equipment\rquote  from the menu, and you can pop on anything in that character's inventory, and even swap stuff in and out of the bag, in which it's best to stow anything you're not going to need immediately in order to avoid unnecessary clutter.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b The Woes of Being Wiped Out\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 If everyone in your party is defeated, you will be wiped out, at which point you will have to choose to return to one of three places: wherever it was you last prayed, the last major location you visited or the last place the game autosaved.\par
\par
If you pick the last place you prayed or visited, you'll keep all the items and experience points collected since you last saved, but lose half of your gold coins. If you choose to return to the last autosave instead, you'll lose any items, experience points and gold coins earned since then, but everything else will remain as is.\par
\par
Whichever one you end up choosing, any gold coins deposited in the Rainbow's End Bank will stay there, safe and sound.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b Beating a Hasty Retreat\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 In battle, more often than not you'll see a white circle surrounding you. Run up to the edge of it, and you'll have the option to flee. However, this won't always work, which could leave you very vulnerable to attack.\par
\par
In certain battles, the circle will be red instead\f1\emdash\f0 that means that you can't escape, no matter how hard you try.\par
\par
If you don't want to run to the white line, you can press  and select \lquote Flee\rquote  from the \lquote Tactics\rquote  menu instead.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
