\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 The speed at which battle unfolds can be adjusted under \lquote Settings\rquote  in the \lquote Tactics\rquote  menu.\par
\par
And don't worry\f1\emdash\f0 no matter what pace you push things to, it won't make the actual difficulty different.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b All About Attributes\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 HP stands for \lquote health points\rquote . These will be depleted when a character takes damage. Try not to let them all be lost, as this will cause the character in question to collapse.\par
\par
MP stands for \lquote magic points\rquote . These are required in order to sling spells or unleash abilities.\par
\par
\lquote Maximum HP\rquote  tells you the total number of health points currently available to a character.\par
\par
\lquote Maximum MP\rquote  tells you the total number of magic points currently available to a character.\par
\par
\lquote Attack\rquote  indicates the efficacy of a character's weapon-based blows. The higher it is, the more damage will be dealt by physical attacks.\par
\par
\lquote Defence\rquote  dictates a character's ability to bear the force of physical attacks. The higher it is, the less damage will be taken from weapon-based blows.\par
\par
\lquote Magical Might\rquote  gives an idea of the efficacy of a character's magical attacks. The higher it is, the more damage will be done by spells and suchlike.\par
\par
\lquote Magical Mending\rquote  indicates the efficacy of a character's health-restoring and revival spells. The higher it is, the better these will be.\par
\par
\lquote Strength\rquote  signifies a character's basic physical forcefulness once the effects of equipment and special abilities are taken out of the equation.\par
\par
\lquote Resilience\rquote  reflects a character's basic resistance to physical blows once the effects of equipment and special abilities are taken out of the equation.\par
\par
\lquote Agility\rquote  governs when a character will get their chance to act in battle. Higher agility also gives a greater chance of avoiding enemy attacks.\par
\par
\lquote Deftness\rquote  determines how likely a character is to catch enemies unaware. Higher deftness also makes it far less hard to flee from battle.\par
\par
\lquote Charm\rquote  indicates the odds of enemies being entranced by a character's appearance, and becoming unable to act as a result.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b All About Ailments\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 Sleep\par
\par
When a character's asleep, they'll be completely open to attack, but the impact of physical force may also be enough to bring them round. Spells, on the other hand, can often work their magic without waking those they target.\par
\par
Bedazzlement and Blindness\par
\par
The Dazzle spell and certain other abilities can blind those they target, causing their attacks to miss the mark. This won't affect their spells, though\f1\emdash\f0 these will still fly straight and true.\par
\par
Beguilement and Confusion\par
\par
Confusion and beguilement can be perplexing indeed, but sometimes all it takes is the short, sharp shock of an attack from an ally to snap someone out of it. No pain, no gain!\par
\par
Poison\par
\par
Persons afflicted with poison will take damage every time their turn comes around, and this unpleasant effect will continue even after the end of battle. The ailment will wear off of its own accord, but is better off being cured with items or abilities.\par
\par
Curses\par
\par
Becoming cursed can cause you to lose your turn in battle, among other unpleasant afflictions. Certain items and abilities can cure it, but if all else fails, you can always seek benediction at a church.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b Mini Medals\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 There's a certain special someone in Erdrea who might just take the mini medals you can find hidden about the place off your hands\f1\emdash\f0 and offer you some really quite rare rewards in exchange.\par
\par
Hunt them down, and all that chest-chasing and chest-of-drawer-rummaging may pay off very handsomely indeed!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b Draconian Quest\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 Opting to undertake a Draconian Quest will allow you to add certain restrictions to your adventure, such as being banned from shops or being unable to put on armour.\par
\par
You'll only be able to begin this brutally challenging new mode by creating a new adventure log altogether, but you can remove your restrictions by visiting a church or sacred statue if things get too tough. However, you can't reapply them without starting all over again\f1\emdash\f0 once they're gone, they're gone.\par
\par
You can try turning them all on at once if you want, but you really don't have to\f1\emdash\f0 finishing with a certain restriction set will see it remain on your record forever, so you're free to take them on one at a time.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b Removing Restrictions\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 You can remove Draconian Quest restrictions whenever you like by visiting a church or sacred statue.\par
\par
You'll then be free to continue your adventure without the removed restrictions, but be aware that you won't be able to reapply them later\f1\emdash\f0 once they're gone, they're gone.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b Draconian Quest Settings\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 If you've undertaken a Draconian Quest, you'll be able to access a section of the menu called \lquote Draconian Quest\rquote  under \lquote System Settings\rquote  in the \lquote Misc.\rquote  menu.\par
\par
Here, you can check which handicaps you currently have enabled, and choose if you want them to be displayed on-screen. Why might you want to do that, you ask? Why, to show off to your friends, of course!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh302\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b Happy Snapping!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 Push  on  or open up the \lquote Quick Commands\rquote  menu to access Photo Mode and record your pals for posterity. You can change the party's poses with , and also alter the line-up, and even who gets to be in the photo.\par
\par
