\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b Fun-Size Forge Fundamentals\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 Smithing items couldn't be simpler\f1\emdash\f0 select \lquote Bash\rquote  to start beating your ingredients into shape, and \lquote Finish\rquote  when you're ready to wrap things up.\par
\par
Hammer away at each individual area with your Portapounder to fill up the blue gauge next to it, and aim to get every gauge into the green zone.\par
\par
See the Traveller's Tips for more information.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b\'b7\~Fun-Size Forge Fundamentals Part I\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b0 Select \lquote Bash\rquote  to start beating your ingredients into shape, and \lquote Finish\rquote  when you're ready to wrap things up.\par
\par
Hammer away at each individual area with your Portapounder to fill up the blue gauge next to it, and aim to get every gauge into the green zone. If you can fill them to the very middle of the green areas, they'll go yellow, producing a piece of the finest possible quality!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10348 
\pard\intbl\b\'b7\~Fun-Size Forge Fundamentals Part II\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
